/-!
# A finite coordinate certificate for the projective orthogonality graph

Base-three integers encode the 117 sign classes of vectors of norm `-1`.
The adjacency rows are bit vectors: bit `j` of row `i` records orthogonality.
The kernel checks the norm, exhaustiveness up to sign, and every adjacency
entry against the quadratic form. The numeric tables are merely certificates;
none of their mathematical properties is assumed.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, §F.5, Lemma F.5.8, printed pp. 303–304.
-/

